build: build dril for headless GBM, not only for GLX/X11

The dril target produces the per-display-driver DRI stubs (sun4i-drm_dri.so,
rockchip_dri.so and friends). gbm_create_device() needs the stub matching the
KMS device it is handed, so on a system with GBM but no X11 and no GLX the
stub is never built and EGL cannot be initialised at all.

This matters specifically for a render-only GPU paired with a display-only KMS
driver, where every GL surface has to be allocated through kmsro against the
display node. On a BananaPi M2 Magic (lima + sun4i-drm, no X11):

  [DRM]: Found 1 connectors. Connector 0 connected: yes. Mode 0: (800x480)
  [KMS]: Couldn't create GBM device.
  [KMS]: Couldn't find a suitable DRM device.
  [Video]: Cannot open video driver.. Exiting..

with /usr/lib/dri empty, while Mesa's own dril/meson.build lists
'sun4i-drm_dri.so' and dril_target.c has DEFINE_LOADER_DRM_ENTRYPOINT(sun4i_drm).
The support is present; only the build gate excludes it.

The enclosing condition is already "with_gallium and with_gbm", so extending the
inner test with with_gbm is the right scope: GLX and X11 are sufficient reasons
to build dril, not necessary ones.

Signed-off-by: RetroBPI_M2M

--- a/src/meson.build
+++ b/src/meson.build
@@ -154,7 +154,17 @@
   subdir('egl')
 endif
 if with_gallium and with_gbm
-  if with_glx == 'dri' or with_platform_x11 or with_platform_xcb
+  # The dril target is what produces the per-display-driver DRI stubs such as
+  # sun4i-drm_dri.so, and gbm_create_device() needs one for the KMS device it
+  # is given. Gating it on GLX/X11 leaves a headless KMS system with GBM but no
+  # stub, so EGL cannot be brought up on a render-only GPU paired with a
+  # display-only KMS driver (lima + sun4i-drm, panfrost + a KMS-only display,
+  # and so on): gbm_create_device() simply fails.
+  #
+  # This block is already inside "if with_gallium and with_gbm", so building
+  # dril whenever GBM is enabled is the correct scope -- X11 and GLX are
+  # sufficient reasons, not necessary ones.
+  if with_glx == 'dri' or with_platform_x11 or with_platform_xcb or with_gbm
     subdir('gallium/targets/dril')
   endif
 endif
